# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Mustfile — release-blocking invariants for Hermeneia
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: must.ncl
# The runner schema expects `probe` (not `run`) and treats failures as blocking.
#
# This is a project-specific draft. The compatible contractile CLI is not
# bundled here, so do not claim `must check` is an active command. The local
# structural subset is enforced by scripts/verify-contractiles.sh and CI;
# Rust and end-to-end tests are enforced by the workflows named below.

@abstract:
Hermeneia's hard requirements are about an honest and safe query-language
slice: complete cross-referenced tridents, reproducible repository rendering,
passing workspace tests, and the end-to-end invoke path checked against the
real external oracle. CI enforcement is deliberately described per probe;
file presence alone does not mean every declaration is already wired to a
contractile runtime.
@end

## Repository and Trident Integrity

### project-entry-points
- description: The project identity, applied specification, source workspace, and core status record are present
- probe: test -f README.adoc && test -f EXPLAINME.adoc && test -f docs/SPEC.adoc && test -f Cargo.toml && test -f Cargo.lock && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml
- severity: critical

### workspace-crates-present
- description: All five Hermeneia workspace crates remain present
- probe: for crate in hermeneia-ir hermeneia-syntax hermeneia-store hermeneia-core hermeneia-cli; do test -f "src/$crate/Cargo.toml" || exit 1; done
- severity: critical

### contractile-tridents-complete
- description: Each of the six Hermeneia contractiles has a declaration, runner, K9 component, manifest, reciprocal links, and matching content hashes
- probe: bash scripts/verify-contractiles.sh
- severity: critical
- notes: The probe is a structural check. It does not parse K9/Nickel or ratify policy.

### rendered-instantiation
- description: Rendered project values still match the checked-in instantiation source
- probe: bash scripts/instantiate.sh --check
- severity: critical

### no-unfilled-project-placeholders
- description: No unfilled project substitution token remains in the repository
- probe: bash scripts/check-no-placeholders.sh .
- severity: critical

### coaptation-clause-extraction
- description: The Coaptation atomizer emits clauses from all six Xfiles and reports all six provenance entries rather than silently producing an empty inventory
- probe: set -o pipefail; bash .machine_readable/coaptation/extract-clauses.sh .machine_readable/contractiles | jq -e '(.clauses | length > 0) and (([.clauses[].verb] | unique | length) == 6) and (any(.clauses[]; .verb == "intend" and .is_wish)) and (all(.clauses[]; (.description | length) > 0)) and ((.provenance | keys | length) == 6)' >/dev/null
- severity: critical
- notes: This checks extraction only; Coaptation receipt comparison still requires Nickel and the generated receipt must not be hand-edited.

## Executable Slice

### workspace-tests
- description: All local unit and integration tests pass
- probe: cargo test --workspace
- severity: critical
- notes: Enforced by Rust CI. Requires the Rust toolchain.

### oracle-backed-invoke-slice
- description: The same invoke path passes against the real trope-checker oracle; missing oracle is a failure, not a skip
- probe: cargo test -p hermeneia-cli --features e2e --test slice
- severity: critical
- notes: The Slice workflow builds tropecheck-rs and supplies HERMENEIA_TROPECHECK. A bare local invocation needs that environment variable.

### no-fabricated-loss-or-verdict
- description: Unsupported vokes, checker absence, malformed store data, and unavailable loss output fail honestly rather than yielding a fabricated success
- probe: cargo test --workspace
- severity: critical
- notes: Covers the parser/core/store unit tests and the always-on workflow gate that keeps the oracle-backed slice enabled.
